    "slug": "igcse-revision-with-et-ai",
    "title": "IGCSE Revision with ET AI: A Step-by-Step Plan",
    "excerpt": "Plan IGCSE revision with ET AI: turn your notes into a day-by-day plan to exam day, practise with ET Maths and ET Exams, and get essays graded on the 9-1 scale.",
    "body": "To revise for IGCSE with ET AI, add your notes to Exam Prep and it builds a day-by-day plan that ends on your exam date, with lessons, quizzes and a full mock. Use your subject's ET AI teacher, such as ET Maths or ET Biology, for explanations, and ET AI Essay Writer for written work graded on the 9-1 scale.\n\n## Why IGCSE revision needs a plan, not just more hours\n\nIGCSE exam season has a way of arriving all at once. You might be sitting several subjects, each with its own syllabus, papers and command words, and your notes are probably spread across exercise books, handouts, photos on your phone and half-finished flashcards. Working longer hours rarely fixes that. What helps is a plan that starts from your exam dates and works backwards, mixing learning, self-testing and at least one full practice paper.\n\nThat's how Poket School approaches revision. ET AI doesn't just answer questions. It helps you plan, practise and track how well you really understand each topic. Poket School also follows one simple principle: *we supplement, we do not replace*. It works alongside your school, tutor or self-study programme, not instead of it.\n\nHere's a step-by-step way to use it for IGCSE revision.\n\n## Step 1: Know your board and your syllabus\n\nBefore you revise anything, check which exam board and syllabus you're sitting. Ask your school or check the board's own website. Cambridge International (CAIE), Pearson Edexcel and Oxford AQA all offer IGCSE or International GCSE qualifications, and their content and papers differ.\n\nPoket School content is aligned to CAIE syllabuses across Primary, IGCSE and A-Level, and to Pearson Edexcel IGCSE. It also supports Oxford AQA International GCSE programmes. One important point: Poket School isn't affiliated with, endorsed by or accredited by CAIE, Pearson Edexcel, Oxford AQA or any other exam board. Think of it as a study partner aligned to your syllabus, and always treat your board's official specification as the final word.\n\n## Step 2: Turn your notes into a day-by-day plan with Exam Prep\n\nOnce you know what you're revising, let Exam Prep do the scheduling. Add your own notes and Exam Prep turns them into a day-by-day plan that ends on your exam date. Each plan mixes lessons, quizzes and a full mock, so you aren't just re-reading. You're testing yourself as you go.\n\nBecause the plan runs to the exam date, topics come back over time rather than being covered once and forgotten. A focus timer sits on each goal, which makes it easier to start a session and see it through. If you have several exams, build a plan for each subject so every paper gets the time it needs.\n\n## Step 3: Learn each topic with your ET AI teacher\n\nWhen a topic doesn't make sense, ask a specialist. Poket School has 30+ ET AI teachers, each named ET plus a subject, and they're available 24/7 by voice or text. For IGCSE, that includes ET Biology, ET Chemistry, ET Physics, ET Maths, ET Additional Maths, ET English, ET History, ET Geography, ET Economics, ET Business Studies, ET Computer Science and more.\n\nEach teacher focuses on what its subject actually rewards. ET History works on source evaluation and extended writing, aiming for marks for analysis rather than just recall. ET Economics teaches the logic of a diagram before the theory. ET Chemistry explains the *why* behind each reaction, not just the formula. If you're stuck at night or the weekend before a paper, you don't have to wait for your next lesson.\n\n### Cross-subject help: ET Exam Coach and ET Study Coach\n\nSome revision problems aren't about one subject. ET Exam Coach works across all subjects on exam technique, time management, decoding questions and revision planning. ET Study Coach is your accountability partner for goal setting, daily plans, learning habits and motivation. Use ET Exam Coach when you keep losing marks on how you answer, and ET Study Coach when the problem is getting started at all.\n\n## Step 4: Practise maths with ET Maths\n\nMaths is learned by doing, and ET Maths is built for that. Snap a photo of a problem or type it in, and ET Maths will walk you through it step by step, or show a full worked solution if you want to check your answer.\n\nFor revision, try each problem yourself first, then use the step-by-step walkthrough to see where your method went wrong. Keep the full solution for checking, so you practise the method rather than reading answers. If you're taking extended or additional maths, ET Additional Maths covers functions, calculus, trigonometry and advanced algebra.\n\n## Step 5: Mix up your formats with ET AI Studio\n\nIf re-reading the same notes isn't working, change the format. Upload your notes or a photo of a textbook page, and ET AI Studio can turn it into lessons, quizzes, mind maps, audio and more, across 11 learning formats.\n\nA mind map can help you see how a Geography topic fits together, an audio summary lets you review Biology on the bus, and an interactive quiz turns a page of Chemistry notes into active recall. Using several formats keeps revision fresh and gives you more chances to test yourself on the same material.\n\n## Step 6: Get feedback on your writing and practise full papers\n\nWritten answers are where many students lose marks without knowing why. ET AI Essay Writer grades written work on the 9-1 and A*-U scales, so you can submit an essay or extended answer, see where it sits and work on the next draft.\n\nFor exam practice, ET Exams generates questions to the syllabus, and Exam Prep plans end with a full mock. One thing to be clear about: official past papers aren't copied into Poket School. Past papers in the exam centre are licensed or uploaded by a teacher, and board papers remain the exam board's copyright. Keep working through official past papers from your school or board alongside the practice ET AI gives you.\n\n## Step 7: Track how deeply you understand each topic\n\nFeeling familiar with a topic isn't the same as being able to answer an exam question on it. Poket School's Bloom's mastery tracker shows how deeply you understand each subject across six cognitive levels, topic by topic, from remembering facts to applying and evaluating them.\n\nCheck it at the end of each week. Topics stuck at the lower levels are where your next revision sessions should go. Feed them back into your plan, test yourself again and watch them move up.\n\n## What's included for IGCSE students\n\nThe IGCSE & A-Level plan covers IGCSE, A-Level and Pre-University. It costs $79 a month or $708 a year, at one flat price worldwide, and you can cancel any time. It includes ET AI Studio, ET Maths and ET Exams, ET AI Essay Writer, unlimited ET AI tutoring and Bloom's progress tracking.\n\nIf you'd like to look around first, the Free Preview costs nothing and needs no card. You can browse the course catalogue, take the first lesson of any course and send the ET AI tutor 20 messages a day. Students who want real-time face-to-face sessions can add ET AI Live, where an AI teacher sees and hears you.\n\n## A sample week of IGCSE revision\n\nHere's one illustrative way to put the steps together in a week:\n\n- **Monday:** learn a new Biology topic with ET Biology, then take an ET AI Studio quiz on it.\n- **Tuesday:** work through five maths problems on your own, then check them with ET Maths step by step.\n- **Wednesday:** write one History extended answer and get it graded by ET AI Essay Writer.\n- **Thursday:** follow your Exam Prep plan for Chemistry, mixing in questions from earlier topics.\n- **Friday:** listen to an audio summary of the week's weakest topic.\n- **Weekend:** check your Bloom's mastery tracker and adjust next week's plan.\n\nAdjust it to your own subjects and exam dates. The point is a steady rhythm of learning, testing and reviewing, rather than one long cram.",
